+INDEPENDENT STAGE 3 CLASSIFICATION
+
+Frozen verification file:
+  /reference/k-proof/verification.k
+  sha256 faca9c79e3e682c7c55c83a5a3d8488cd94981b6a0a22672628775aaed76ac9e
+
+Trusted reconstructed local verification-module closure:
+  modules: [VERIFICATION]
+  ordered rule count: 10
+  inventory sha256:
+    60eb713b2b76c3b7c275bba937b7723b878edafd277c1b79e528ce79ab39b6fd
+
+Judgment by frozen source order:
+
+1. rule-8bcfa7361e04eeb6225dd92057dababa4bf93ef43bff859c938d6dddf981efe3
+   lines 9-9, onlyStrings(.ValSeq) => true
+   CLASSIFICATION: DEFINITION
+   Reason: base equation of the named recursive Boolean summary onlyStrings.
+
+2. rule-12afafd0a0521f95ae4bb41974ef61175f0db0e7f53b5a8ab64abe0ab0182442
+   lines 10-11, recursive onlyStrings equation
+   CLASSIFICATION: DEFINITION
+   Reason: recursive equation of the named summary onlyStrings.
+
+3. rule-8b66a93eec9276b2d742ed7c9ecef3b7815fa8a02a34fe20adb5d747be019300
+   line 16, stringCodes(str(CS)) => CS
+   CLASSIFICATION: DEFINITION
+   Reason: principal projection equation of the named helper stringCodes.
+
+4. rule-15462c50b7340ac165d712c183d20f39114256f0a77864f57113d62121d4b835
+   line 17, stringCodes(_V) => .IntSeq [owise]
+   CLASSIFICATION: DEFINITION
+   Reason: fallback equation completing the named helper stringCodes. The
+   arbitrary fallback outside string inputs does not turn this defining
+   equation into a theorem about the source program.
+
+5. rule-b3f45b5d74172f8b06aeed730c933057ce5ded1254eac17997dee1565ec954d1
+   lines 21-23:
+     seqLen(V) => isLen(stringCodes(V))
+       requires isStrV(V)
+       [simplification]
+   CLASSIFICATION: DOMAIN_LEMMA
+   Reason: this is not a defining equation for a new summary. It connects the
+   pre-existing operational observer seqLen to the separately defined
+   projection stringCodes and pre-existing isLen, under the string guard. It
+   is not an ordinary execution rule, and Stage 1 did not first prove the
+   exact rule against a module omitting it before using it; therefore it is
+   neither OPERATIONAL_RULE nor PROVED_DERIVED_LEMMA. It is the sole
+   [simplification] rule, so its DOMAIN_LEMMA classification is permitted.
+
+6. rule-1bba7b86c835e7afed82818697a61da1c1a640f585771c5451e6a4797d223cc7
+   line 28, totalLen(ITEMS) => totalLenFrom(0, ITEMS)
+   CLASSIFICATION: DEFINITION
+   Reason: wrapper equation of the named total-length summary.
+
+7. rule-ad39b76bc1e390fe2c642f62148031564aba628ffb8a4e6671eac35ea5830b19
+   line 29, base totalLenFrom equation
+   CLASSIFICATION: DEFINITION
+   Reason: base equation of the named accumulator recurrence.
+
+8. rule-59d7919df49851f487a751100aea360abb2cc715fcf4747dbb11d037bb2b45eb
+   lines 30-31, recursive totalLenFrom equation
+   CLASSIFICATION: DEFINITION
+   Reason: recursive equation of the named accumulator recurrence.
+
+9. rule-5003da3d7156c8d67318d1d506c428d29a27f6057012a2b10ef5b4a0bc66f7a0
+   line 35, base lastLoopValue equation
+   CLASSIFICATION: DEFINITION
+   Reason: base equation of the named loop-result summary.
+
+10. rule-7e6a81b0c0557e15b86a153b9eb772fac0540f01be79e9675941cdf9d95ffb3f
+    lines 36-37, recursive lastLoopValue equation
+    CLASSIFICATION: DEFINITION
+    Reason: recursive equation of the named loop-result summary.
+
+True domain set:
+  exactly {
+    rule-b3f45b5d74172f8b06aeed730c933057ce5ded1254eac17997dee1565ec954d1
+  }
+
+Relevance and truth of the domain lemma:
+  The source program calls len(item) on items accepted as strings. The
+  postcondition's totalLen recurrence accumulates isLen(stringCodes(V)).
+  Frozen operational semantics says that direct string values satisfy isStrV,
+  seqLen(str(IS)) reduces to isLen(IS), and stringCodes(str(IS)) reduces to
+  IS. Hence the guarded equation is true, directly bridges execution to the
+  postcondition summary, and is load-bearing rather than irrelevant.
+
+Comparison with protected classification:
+  The protected manifest assigns DEFINITION to entries 1-4 and 6-10 and
+  DOMAIN_LEMMA to entry 5. It contains no OPERATIONAL_RULE or
+  PROVED_DERIVED_LEMMA entries. The independent classifications therefore
+  agree entry-for-entry, for substantive reasons rather than reliance on the
+  protected labels.

apply patch
